# VS Code: keep shared launch/task definitions, ignore per-user state.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json

## NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json

## Secrets and local state
#
# The Steam Web API key lives in one of these two and must never be committed.
# user-settings.json is what the in-app Settings page writes; it normally sits in
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\OhMyLibrary, but a stray copy in the working tree would carry a
# live key straight into the repository.
appsettings.local.json
appsettings.*.local.json
user-settings.json
secrets.json
*.local.env

## Local runtime data
#
# Scoped deliberately: an unscoped *.db would also swallow a test fixture or a
# seed database that a future change legitimately needs to track.
library.db
library.db-shm
library.db-wal
window.json
imagecache/

